                <pb facs="0773" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5747/6–7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-04-08"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root, referring to dispatch of February 22 last, says it is believed it
                    would facilitate matters if the Panaman Government would authorize Minister
                    Arango to take up with the department the question of selecting an umpire.
                    Instructs Mr. Squiers to interview the minister for foreign affairs and
                    ascertain his views on this point.)</p>
            </div>
